IMPORT prelude

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (NT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL), not the daydate library. The Act fixes no
-- period of its own. The one deadline a party meets is the time the Supreme Court sets when it directs a party to give
-- the Attorneys-General notice of a special federal matter (s 6(5)(b)); it is counted here in plain days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory; quoted under the NT
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). This is not an official version of the Act.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (NT)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`
